  "narrative": "All returned estimates are already signed to their registered directions. For feature_027 direction +1, a positive mean_difference means feature_027=1 has a higher, less negative CRISPR dependency score than feature_027=0, i.e. weaker measured dependency. The dominant result remains feature_027 for outcome_014. H84 within feature_042=1 gives +0.794 [0.752, 0.837], with cell sizes 75 and 388; this is far above the approximate outcome_014 10%-scale reference near 0.0093, so I accept it as a dataset-specific association. H95 within feature_009 level_003 gives +0.796 [0.772, 0.819], also far above threshold and feasible, so I accept it. Together with H80 within feature_042=0 and validated H70, this strongly supports a very large feature_027/outcome_014 association that is not confined to feature_042=0 or to the largest feature_009 stratum. However, because the effect is enormous and outcome-specific, it should be interpreted as a measured predictor/artifact/stratification structure in this supplied dataset, not as a causal or externally generalizable biological mechanism. H94 tests positive interaction of feature_027 by feature_042=1 on outcome_014 and gives -0.0024 [-0.0507, 0.0458]. This does not support a clinically meaningful positive interaction; it is near null, though its interval includes both directions because feature_042=1 and feature_027=1 overlap is modest. I reject the registered positive-interaction direction but note that this does not prove exact absence of all effect modification. The outcome-specificity panel mostly argues against broad feature_027 spread across dependency outcomes. H86 outcome_015, H87 outcome_002, H88 outcome_016, H91 outcome_003, H92 outcome_008, and H93 outcome_011 have registered positive direction estimates small and opposite or near zero, with upper bounds below their approximate 10% thresholds, so I reject those positive weaker-dependency directions. H85 outcome_005, H89 outcome_009, and H90 outcome_010 have point estimates below their approximate 10% thresholds and intervals that include both non-meaningful and potentially meaningful positive values, so they remain unresolved but are deferred because they are much weaker than the outcome_014 signal. The proposed feature_027 main effect within feature_009 level_001 is a low-burden follow-up to the accepted level_003 effect and the registered level_001 interaction; it will be discarded if cell sizes are insufficient. I request validation of H84 because it completes the feature_027/feature_042 conditional structure but has the smallest feature_027=1 cell among these subgroup contrasts, so independent replication is useful to rule out a sparse conditional anomaly.",
  "research_notes": "Round 7 appraise update: feature_027/outcome_014 is a very large, robust dataset-specific association. It remains huge in feature_042=0 (H80), feature_042=1 (H84), and feature_009 level_003 (H95), and the direct positive feature_027-by-feature_042 interaction H94 is near null. The strongest interpretation is that feature_027 is a powerful measured predictor/artifact/stratification signal for outcome_014 in this dataset, with possible partial secondary signals in outcome_013, outcome_006, and weak unresolved signals in outcome_005/009/010; it is not currently supported as a broad clinically meaningful artifact across most other outcomes. H38/feature_042 should remain demoted as a marginal unadjusted association only; conditional feature_042 effects within feature_027 strata and the interaction do not support it as an independent predictor. Next: validate H84 because of small exposed cell in feature_042=1 and feature_027=1; run H96-H103 plus proposed feature_027 within feature_009 level_001. Avoid claiming causality or external generalizability.",
